{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc | sed -n '1,460p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '160,270p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc | sed -n '1,250p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.space.store\n     2\t  \"The durable directory store of a covered code index\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md, \\\"Durable store\\\"): one\n     4\t   directory holding `content.jing` — the `dao.jing.file` content log a\n     5\t   publisher's blobs materialize into — `HEAD`, the versioned record\n     6\t   naming the latest published manifest, and `lock`, the exclusive lock.\n     7\t\n     8\t   `open` is exclusive and validating: the lock (dao.space.store.fs) is\n     9\t   acquired before anything else in the directory is touched and held\n    10\t   until `close!`; HEAD is read and the snapshot it names walked in full\n    11\t   through the opened store (`dao.space.index/read-manifest`, every index\n    12\t   root), so an absent HEAD is an empty index while a malformed HEAD, a\n    13\t   missing manifest, or an unreadable index node refuses rather than\n    14\t   opening empty.  A publisher moves HEAD with `:head-fn` only after its\n    15\t   manifest reads back, and what the open recovered is `:recovery`.\n    16\t\n    17\t   It lives in `dao.space` because HEAD names a covered-index manifest and\n    18\t   opening validates that index; `dao.jing` stays payload-agnostic.  Its\n    19\t   consumers are `dao.space.dht/join` (`:dir`) and the REPL's `file:<dir>`\n    20\t   and `dht:<dir>` stores (yin.repl.store).\"\n    21\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n    22\t                       [clojure.edn :as edn]])\n    23\t            #?(:cljd nil\n    24\t               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    25\t               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n    26\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    27\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    28\t            [dao.jing.file :as jing.file]\n    29\t            [dao.space.index :as dao.index]\n    30\t            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def content-name\n    34\t  \"The content log's own file name inside a durable store directory.\"\n    35\t  \"content.jing\")\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(def head-name\n    39\t  \"The durable root pointer's own file name inside a durable store\n    40\t   directory: the versioned record naming the latest published\n    41\t   manifest.\"\n    42\t  \"HEAD\")\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(def head-version\n    46\t  \"The HEAD record version this store writes and accepts.\"\n    47\t  1)\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(def unsupported-host-text\n    51\t  \"The refusal for a durable directory on a host build that cannot open\n    52\t   files.  Refusing is the contract: a build without a filesystem is never\n    53\t   answered with an in-memory store its caller did not choose.\"\n    54\t  (str \"a durable store directory is not supported on this host: opening \"\n    55\t       \"the content log needs a filesystem, and this build has none; use \"\n    56\t       \"an in-memory store, or run on a host with file support (the JVM, \"\n    57\t       \"Node, or Dart)\"))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn host-file-support\n    61\t  \"True when this build can open a file-backed store: the JVM, Node, and\n    62\t   Dart can; a CLJS build without `js/require` cannot.\"\n    63\t  []\n    64\t  #?(:cljd true\n    65\t     :cljs (exists? js/require)\n    66\t     :clj true))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- without-trailing-separator\n    70\t  \"The directory path with any trailing `/` removed, so the content log's\n    71\t   path is joined exactly once.  A path of only separators names the root,\n    72\t   which is preserved.\"\n    73\t  [dir]\n    74\t  (loop [s dir]\n    75\t    (if (and (pos? (count s)) (= \"/\" (subs s (dec (count s)))))\n    76\t      (recur (subs s 0 (dec (count s))))\n    77\t      s)))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn content-path\n    81\t  \"The content log's own path inside the store directory:\n    82\t   `<dir>/content.jing`.\"\n    83\t  [dir]\n    84\t  (let [base (without-trailing-separator dir)]\n    85\t    (if (str/blank? base)\n    86\t      (str \"/\" content-name)\n    87\t      (str base \"/\" content-name))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- error-text\n    91\t  \"The host error's own message, for the tail of a refusal.\"\n    92\t  [e]\n    93\t  #?(:cljd (str e)\n    94\t     :clj (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n    95\t     :cljs (or (ex-message e) (str e))))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn- dir-refusal\n    99\t  \"Why `dir` cannot hold the durable content log, or nil when it can: a\n   100\t   path occupied by something that is not a directory, a directory this\n   101\t   process cannot write, or a directory that cannot be created.  Nothing\n   102\t   is opened here — the content log itself is opened later, and its open\n   103\t   failure is refused with its own reason.\"\n   104\t  [dir]\n   105\t  #?(:cljd (let [d (dart-io/Directory. dir)\n   106\t                 f (dart-io/File. dir)]\n   107\t             (cond\n   108\t               (.existsSync d) nil\n   109\t               (.existsSync f) (str dir \" is not a directory\")\n   110\t               :else (try (.createSync d .recursive true)\n   111\t                          nil\n   112\t                          (catch Object e\n   113\t                            (str \"cannot create \" dir \": \" (error-text e))))))\n   114\t     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. dir)]\n   115\t            (cond\n   116\t              (and (.exists f) (not (.isDirectory f)))\n   117\t              (str dir \" is not a directory\")\n   118\t\n   119\t              (and (.isDirectory f) (not (.canWrite f)))\n   120\t              (str dir \" is not writable\")\n   121\t\n   122\t              :else\n   123\t              (try (when (and (not (.isDirectory f)) (not (.mkdirs f)))\n   124\t                     (str \"cannot create \" dir))\n   125\t                   (catch Exception e\n   126\t                     (str \"cannot create \" dir \": \" (error-text e))))))\n   127\t     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")]\n   128\t             (if (.existsSync fs dir)\n   129\t               (when-not (.isDirectory (.statSync fs dir))\n   130\t                 (str dir \" is not a directory\"))\n   131\t               (try (.mkdirSync fs dir #js {:recursive true})\n   132\t                    nil\n   133\t                    (catch :default e\n   134\t                      (str \"cannot create \" dir \": \" (error-text e))))))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn file-refusal\n   138\t  \"Why a `file:<dir>` store cannot open, or nil when it can: a host without\n   139\t   file support is named first — never answered with a memory fallback —\n   140\t   then the directory's own refusal.  The one-argument arity asks this\n   141\t   build's own capability; the two-argument one answers for the capability\n   142\t   it is handed, which is how the unsupported-host refusal is tested on\n   143\t   hosts that do have file support.\"\n   144\t  ([dir] (file-refusal (host-file-support) dir))\n   145\t  ([capable? dir]\n   146\t   (or (when-not capable? unsupported-host-text)\n   147\t       (dir-refusal dir))))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn- head-record\n   151\t  \"The text of one HEAD record: the version and the manifest address,\n   152\t   written whole and replaced whole.\"\n   153\t  [manifest-address]\n   154\t  (str (pr-str {:version head-version :manifest manifest-address}) \"\\n\"))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn- read-edn\n   158\t  [text]\n   159\t  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n   160\t     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n   161\t     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- recovered-head\n   165\t  \"The manifest address HEAD names, or nil for an empty index.  A missing\n   166\t   file is an empty index; a file that is not exactly the versioned\n   167\t   record naming a content address is a corrupt pointer, and a corrupt\n   168\t   pointer refuses startup rather than pretending there was no index.\"\n   169\t  [dir]\n   170\t  (if-some [text (fs/read-file-text dir head-name)]\n   171\t    (let [head (try (read-edn text)\n   172\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   173\t                              :clj Exception\n   174\t                              :cljs :default)\n   175\t                           e\n   176\t                      (throw (ex-info (str \"the HEAD at \" dir\n   177\t                                           \" is not a readable record: \"\n   178\t                                           (error-text e))\n   179\t                                      {:dir dir :head text}\n   180\t                                      e))))]\n   181\t      (when-not (and (map? head)\n   182\t                     (= head-version (:version head))\n   183\t                     (jing/segment-address? (:manifest head)))\n   184\t        (throw (ex-info (str \"the HEAD at \" dir \" is not a version-\"\n   185\t                             head-version\n   186\t                             \" record naming a manifest address\")\n   187\t                        {:dir dir :head head})))\n   188\t      (:manifest head))\n   189\t    nil))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- validated-snapshot\n   193\t  \"The datoms of the snapshot HEAD names, walked eagerly through the\n   194\t   opened store — the design's full read-manifest and read-datoms\n   195\t   traversal, over every index root the manifest names, not only EAVT:\n   196\t   each of the four trees must read back whole and cover exactly the\n   197\t   manifest's `:count` datoms.  A missing or invalid manifest, or any\n   198\t   unreadable index node, refuses startup here; never a silent empty\n   199\t   index.\"\n   200\t  [store dir manifest-address]\n   201\t  (try\n   202\t    (let [manifest (dao.index/read-manifest store manifest-address)\n   203\t          walked (into {}\n   204\t                       (map (fn [[index root]]\n   205\t                              [index (vec (dao.index/walk-index-datoms\n   206\t                                            store root))]))\n   207\t                       (:indexes manifest))]\n   208\t      (doseq [[index datoms] walked]\n   209\t        (when-not (= (:count manifest) (count datoms))\n   210\t          (throw (ex-info (str \"the \" (name index) \" index covers \"\n   211\t                               (count datoms) \" datoms, not the manifest's \"\n   212\t                               (:count manifest))\n   213\t                          {:index index}))))\n   214\t      (:eavt walked))\n   215\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   216\t              :clj Throwable\n   217\t              :cljs :default)\n   218\t           e\n   219\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"the durable index at \" dir \" is corrupt: \"\n   220\t                           (error-text e))\n   221\t                      {:dir dir :manifest manifest-address}\n   222\t                      e)))))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\t(defn- open-locked-dir\n   226\t  \"Open the durable directory as its one owner: take the lock before\n   227\t   anything else in the directory is touched, then open the content log,\n   228\t   read HEAD, and walk the snapshot it names.  Every failure after the\n   229\t   lock closes the content log it opened and releases the lock again, so\n   230\t   a refused startup never leaves this process holding a directory it\n   231\t   did not open.\"\n   232\t  [dir]\n   233\t  (let [lock (fs/lock! dir)\n   234\t        opened (volatile! nil)]\n   235\t    (try\n   236\t      (let [handle (try (jing.file/create-content-file (content-path dir))\n   237\t                        (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   238\t                                  :clj Exception\n   239\t                                  :cljs :default)\n   240\t                               e\n   241\t                          (throw (ex-info (str \"cannot open the index store at \"\n   242\t                                               (content-path dir) \": \"\n   243\t                                               (error-text e))\n   244\t                                          {:dir dir}\n   245\t                                          e))))\n   246\t            _ (vreset! opened handle)\n   247\t            manifest (recovered-head dir)\n   248\t            datoms (when manifest\n   249\t                     (validated-snapshot handle dir manifest))]\n   250\t        {:handle handle\n   251\t         :lock lock\n   252\t         :recovery {:manifest manifest\n   253\t                    :datoms datoms}})\n   254\t      (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   255\t                :clj Throwable\n   256\t                :cljs :default)\n   257\t             e\n   258\t        (when-some [close-content! (:close-fn @opened)]\n   259\t          (try (close-content!)\n   260\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   261\t                         :clj Throwable\n   262\t                         :cljs :default)\n   263\t                      _\n   264\t                 nil)))\n   265\t        (fs/unlock! lock)\n   266\t        (throw e)))))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn lock-releasing-close\n   270\t  \"The durable handle's `:close-fn`: close the content log, then release\n   271\t   the directory lock `lock` — released even when the close throws, so a\n   272\t   failed close never keeps a live process holding the directory.\"\n   273\t  [close-content! lock]\n   274\t  (fn []\n   275\t    (try\n   276\t      (close-content!)\n   277\t      (finally\n   278\t        (fs/unlock! lock)))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t(defn open\n   282\t  \"Open `dir` as a durable directory store, exclusively and validating:\n   283\t   the directory lock is acquired before the content log or HEAD is\n   284\t   touched — a second owner, in this process or another, is refused\n   285\t   naming the directory — and every failure after it releases the lock\n   286\t   again.  HEAD is read and the snapshot it names walked in full: an\n   287\t   absent HEAD is an empty index; a malformed HEAD or a corrupt snapshot\n   288\t   refuses rather than opening empty.  A directory this host cannot open\n   289\t   is refused with its reason.\n   290\t\n   291\t   The handle is the content log's plain byte-store fns plus what its\n   292\t   lifecycle owns: `:close-fn`, which releases the lock with the content\n   293\t   log; `:head-fn`, `(fn [manifest-address])`, the atomic HEAD write a\n   294\t   publisher performs after its manifest reads back; `:recovery`,\n   295\t   `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the walked snapshot or nil>}`;\n   296\t   and `:durable-dir`.\"\n   297\t  [dir]\n   298\t  (if-some [refusal (file-refusal dir)]\n   299\t    (throw (ex-info refusal {:dir dir}))\n   300\t    (let [{:keys [handle lock recovery]} (open-locked-dir dir)]\n   301\t      (assoc handle\n   302\t             :close-fn (lock-releasing-close (:close-fn handle) lock)\n   303\t             :head-fn (fn publish-head!\n   304\t                        [manifest-address]\n   305\t                        (fs/atomic-replace!\n   306\t                          dir head-name\n   307\t                          (head-record manifest-address)))\n   308\t             :recovery recovery\n   309\t             :durable-dir dir))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn durable?\n   313\t  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store `open` answered (or a\n   314\t   handle composed over one, carrying its `:durable-dir`): its published\n   315\t   index outlives the process.\"\n   316\t  [store]\n   317\t  (some? (:durable-dir store)))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t(defn close!\n   321\t  \"Release a store's lifecycle resources — its content log handle and,\n   322\t   for a durable directory, the directory lock.  Nothing further can be read or\n   323\t   written through the handle afterwards.  Idempotent.\"\n   324\t  [store]\n   325\t  (when-let [close! (:close-fn store)]\n   326\t    (close!)))\n   160\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key ring-capacity})))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- oldest\n   164\t  [handle]\n   165\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle :dao.stream/oldest)))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn- local-store\n   169\t  \"The node's local store: the caller's `:local`, or the durable\n   170\t   directory store `dao.space.store/open` opens exclusively at `:dir`.\"\n   171\t  [{:keys [local dir]}]\n   172\t  (or local (durable/open dir)))\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\t(defn- node-over\n   176\t  \"The node composed from checked `opts` over the opened `local` store.\"\n   177\t  [opts local]\n   178\t  (let [{:keys [peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes bind!]} opts\n   179\t          [requests answers facts ticks traffic ledger] (repeatedly 6 ring)\n   180\t          socket? (boolean (seq peers))\n   181\t          composition (cond-> {:local local\n   182\t                               :requests requests\n   183\t                               :answers answers\n   184\t                               :facts facts\n   185\t                               :ticks ticks\n   186\t                               ::dht/id (dht/bytes->hex\n   187\t                                          (secure-random-bytes dht/id-length))\n   188\t                               ::dht/publish? publish?\n   189\t                               ::dht/bootstrap (vec peers)\n   190\t                               ::dht/bind-host bind-host}\n   191\t                        socket? (assoc :traffic traffic\n   192\t                                       ::dht/secret (secure-random-bytes\n   193\t                                                      secret-length)\n   194\t                                       ::dht/max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes))\n   195\t          seam (when socket?\n   196\t                 (bind! {:identity (str \"dao.space.dht:\"\n   197\t                                        (subs (::dht/id composition) 0 16))\n   198\t                         :deposit traffic\n   199\t                         :bind-host bind-host\n   200\t                         :bind-port bind-port\n   201\t                         :max-bytes (::dht/max-datagram dht/defaults)}))\n   202\t          front (dht/store-handle\n   203\t                  {:local local\n   204\t                   :requests requests\n   205\t                   :max-message-bytes (::dht/max-message-bytes dht/defaults)})\n   206\t          closed? (volatile! false)]\n   207\t      {:peers (vec peers)\n   208\t       :publish? publish?\n   209\t       :composition composition\n   210\t       :dht (when-not socket? (dht/state composition))\n   211\t       :seam seam\n   212\t       :traffic-cursor (when socket? (oldest traffic))\n   213\t       :facts (oldest facts)\n   214\t       :ledger ledger\n   215\t       :ledger-cursor (oldest ledger)\n   216\t       :origin nil\n   217\t       :reading nil\n   218\t       :window []\n   219\t       :publications []\n   220\t       :client (content.step/client-state requests answers (oldest answers))\n   221\t       :loads {}\n   222\t       :refusal nil\n   223\t       :handle {:put-bytes-fn (fn [address bs]\n   224\t                               (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn front) address bs)]\n   225\t                                 (stream/append! ledger {::put address})\n   226\t                                 verdict))\n   227\t               :get-bytes-fn (:get-bytes-fn local)\n   228\t               :close-fn (fn []\n   229\t                           (when-not @closed?\n   230\t                             (vreset! closed? true)\n   231\t                             (try (when seam ((:close! seam)))\n   232\t                                  (finally\n   233\t                                    (jing/close! local)))))}}))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn join\n   237\t  \"Join the DHT from `opts` and answer the node:\n   238\t\n   239\t   * `:local` — the node's own `dao.jing` store, already opened (and, if\n   240\t     it is a directory, already locked) by the caller, as `yin.repl` does\n   241\t     — or `:dir`, a directory `join` opens as the durable directory store\n   242\t     (`dao.space.store/open`): exclusively, under the directory lock, so\n   243\t     a second owner in this process or another is refused naming it, and\n   244\t     the lock is held until `close!`;\n   245\t   * `:peers` — bootstrap contacts `[{:host ip :port p} ...]`, none for\n   246\t     solo;\n   247\t   * `:publish?` — whether everything in the local store is public;\n   248\t   * `:bind-host`, `:bind-port` — the socket's address, loopback and\n   249\t     ephemeral by default;\n   250\t   * `:max-inbound-bytes` — the inbound storage bound;\n   251\t   * `:bind!` — the datagram host seam, `default-bind` by default.\n   252\t\n   253\t   Refuses an invalid option with its reason.  The node owns `:local`\n   254\t   from here: `close!` closes it.\"\n   255\t  [opts]\n   256\t  (let [opts (merge defaults {:bind! (default-bind)} opts)]\n   257\t    (when-some [why (option-refusal opts)]\n   258\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.space.dht/join: \" why)\n   259\t                      (dissoc opts :bind! :local))))\n   260\t    (let [local (local-store opts)]\n   261\t      (try\n   262\t        (node-over opts local)\n   263\t        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   264\t          ;; a directory join opened: release it, lock included\n   265\t          (when-not (:local opts) (jing/close! local))\n   266\t          (throw e))))))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn store\n   270\t  \"The node's `dao.jing` byte-store handle: put inserts into the local\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.store\n     2\t  \"Startup selection of the code index's store\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md; the durable-store startup\n     4\t   contract, slices 1-3, and the DHT store of epic S5).\n     5\t\n     6\t   The store is chosen once, before the shell composes: `mem` — a fresh\n     7\t   in-memory `dao.jing` store, today's behaviour — `file:<dir>`, the\n     8\t   durable directory store (dao.space.store), or `dht:<dir>`, that store\n     9\t   with a DHT node composed over it (yin.repl.dht).  This namespace parses\n    10\t   the `--index-store` value, validates the `:index-store-spec` an\n    11\t   embedder may hand `yin.repl/create-state`, and opens the store the\n    12\t   resolved spec names.  Every bad spec — a missing value, an unknown\n    13\t   scheme, an empty directory, a directory that cannot be opened, a host\n    14\t   build without file support — is refused with its reason; nothing falls\n    15\t   back to memory silently.\n    16\t\n    17\t   The durable directory itself — the exclusive lock, HEAD, the validated\n    18\t   snapshot, `:recovery` — is dao.space.store's; this namespace is one of\n    19\t   its consumers.  The shell installs the recovery before it admits any\n    20\t   evaluation (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`), and a durable store\n    21\t   (`durable?`) also carries the index across `(reset)` and VM\n    22\t   selection; the memory store keeps today's empty rebuild.\"\n    23\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    24\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    25\t            [dao.jing.mem :as jing.mem]\n    26\t            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(def file-scheme\n    31\t  \"The `--index-store` scheme prefix naming a durable file store.\"\n    32\t  \"file:\")\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(def dht-scheme\n    36\t  \"The `--index-store` scheme prefix naming the DHT store: the durable\n    37\t   directory store of `file:<dir>` composed under a `dao.jing.dht` node\n    38\t   (yin.repl.dht).\"\n    39\t  \"dht:\")\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(def ^:private supported-args\n    43\t  [\"mem\" (str file-scheme \"<dir>\") (str dht-scheme \"<dir>\")])\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn parse-arg\n    47\t  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec: `:mem`, or `{:type :file :dir dir}`\n    48\t   for `file:<dir>`.  A missing value, an unknown scheme, and an empty\n    49\t   directory are refused here — with the supported forms named — so the\n    50\t   arguments parser can refuse a bad flag before anything composes.\"\n    51\t  [value]\n    52\t  (cond\n    53\t    (nil? value)\n    54\t    (throw (ex-info \"--index-store needs a value: mem, file:<dir> or dht:<dir>\"\n    55\t                    {:supported supported-args}))\n    56\t\n    57\t    (= value \"mem\")\n    58\t    :mem\n    59\t\n    60\t    (str/starts-with? value file-scheme)\n    61\t    (let [dir (subs value (count file-scheme))]\n    62\t      (if (str/blank? dir)\n    63\t        (throw (ex-info \"--index-store file:<dir> needs a directory\"\n    64\t                        {:value value\n    65\t                         :supported supported-args}))\n    66\t        {:type :file :dir dir}))\n    67\t\n    68\t    (str/starts-with? value dht-scheme)\n    69\t    (let [dir (subs value (count dht-scheme))]\n    70\t      (if (str/blank? dir)\n    71\t        (throw (ex-info \"--index-store dht:<dir> needs a directory\"\n    72\t                        {:value value\n    73\t                         :supported supported-args}))\n    74\t        {:type :dht :dir dir}))\n    75\t\n    76\t    :else\n    77\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Unknown --index-store \" (pr-str value)\n    78\t                         \"; supported: mem, file:<dir>, dht:<dir>\")\n    79\t                    {:value value\n    80\t                     :supported supported-args}))))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- dht-refusal\n    84\t  \"Why a `{:type :dht ...}` spec is not a DHT store composition, or nil.\n    85\t   A spec with no peers is solo: it opens no socket, so a manifest to\n    86\t   fetch has nothing to fetch through and is refused rather than\n    87\t   ignored.\"\n    88\t  [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes manifest\n    89\t           bind!]}]\n    90\t  (cond\n    91\t    (not (and (string? dir) (not (str/blank? dir))))\n    92\t    \"--index-store dht:<dir> needs a directory\"\n    93\t\n    94\t    (not (and (vector? peers)\n    95\t              (every? #(and (map? %)\n    96\t                            (datagram/ip-literal? (:host %))\n    97\t                            (datagram/valid-port? (:port %)))\n    98\t                      peers)))\n    99\t    \"DHT peers must be {:host <IP literal> :port <1 to 65535>}\"\n   100\t\n   101\t    (not (boolean? publish?))\n   102\t    \"the DHT publication declaration must be true or false\"\n   103\t\n   104\t    (not (datagram/ip-literal? bind-host))\n   105\t    \"the DHT bind host must be an IP literal\"\n   106\t\n   107\t    (not (and (integer? bind-port) (<= 0 bind-port 65535)))\n   108\t    \"the DHT bind port must be 0 (ephemeral) or 1 to 65535\"\n   109\t\n   110\t    (not (and (integer? max-inbound-bytes) (<= 0 max-inbound-bytes)))\n   111\t    \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes must be a nonnegative integer\"\n   112\t\n   113\t    (and (empty? peers) (some? manifest))\n   114\t    (str \"--dht-manifest needs a --dht-peer to fetch from: with no peers \"\n   115\t         \"the DHT store is solo and opens no socket\")\n   116\t\n   117\t    (not (or (nil? manifest) (jing/segment-address? manifest)))\n   118\t    \"--dht-manifest must be a segment manifest address\"\n   119\t\n   120\t    (not (or (nil? bind!) (fn? bind!)))\n   121\t    \":bind! must be a dao.stream.datagram host seam function\"))\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t(def default-max-inbound-bytes\n   125\t  \"The CLI default of the DHT store's inbound storage bound\n   126\t   (`:dao.jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes`): 64 MiB of payload a publishing\n   127\t   node accepts from peers' `:store` requests before it refuses them\n   128\t   explicitly.  `--dht-max-inbound-bytes` overrides it.\"\n   129\t  (* 64 1024 1024))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(def dht-defaults\n   133\t  \"The DHT store spec's defaults: solo (no peers), publishing off, bound\n   134\t   to loopback on an ephemeral port, the default inbound bound, and no\n   135\t   manifest to hydrate.\"\n   136\t  {:peers []\n   137\t   :publish? false\n   138\t   :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   139\t   :bind-port 0\n   140\t   :max-inbound-bytes default-max-inbound-bytes\n   141\t   :manifest nil})\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn checked-spec\n   145\t  \"Validate an `:index-store-spec` as `yin.repl/create-state` receives it:\n   146\t   nil means the `mem` default, `:mem` names it, and a file store is the\n   147\t   map `{:type :file :dir dir}` with a non-empty directory string.  A DHT\n   148\t   store is `{:type :dht :dir dir}` plus its options, `dht-defaults`\n   149\t   filled in; see yin.repl.dht.  Anything else is refused with the\n   150\t   supported forms named.\"\n   151\t  [spec]\n   152\t  (cond\n   153\t    (nil? spec) :mem\n   154\t    (= :mem spec) :mem\n   155\t    (and (map? spec)\n   156\t         (= :file (:type spec))\n   157\t         (string? (:dir spec))\n   158\t         (not (str/blank? (:dir spec))))\n   159\t    spec\n   160\t\n   161\t    (and (map? spec) (= :dht (:type spec)))\n   162\t    (let [spec (merge dht-defaults spec)]\n   163\t      (if-some [refusal (dht-refusal spec)]\n   164\t        (throw (ex-info refusal {:spec (dissoc spec :bind!)}))\n   165\t        spec))\n   166\t\n   167\t    :else\n   168\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Unknown :index-store-spec \" (pr-str spec)\n   169\t                         \"; supported: :mem, {:type :file :dir <dir>}, \"\n   170\t                         \"{:type :dht :dir <dir> ...}\")\n   171\t                    {:spec spec\n   172\t                     :supported [:mem {:type :file :dir \"<dir>\"}\n   173\t                                 {:type :dht :dir \"<dir>\"}]}))))\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t(defn open\n   177\t  \"Open the store `spec` names and keep it plain: `:mem` (or nil) is a\n   178\t   fresh in-memory `dao.jing` store; `{:type :file :dir dir}` is the\n   179\t   durable directory store at `dir` (dao.space.store/open): exclusive,\n   180\t   validating, its HEAD writer, recovery and lock on the handle.  A spec\n   181\t   this build cannot open is refused with its reason; a `dht:<dir>` spec\n   182\t   is opened by yin.repl.dht, which composes its node over the same\n   183\t   durable store.\"\n   184\t  [spec]\n   185\t  (let [checked (checked-spec spec)]\n   186\t    (case (if (map? checked) (:type checked) checked)\n   187\t      :mem (jing.mem/create-content-mem)\n   188\t      :file (durable/open (:dir checked))\n   189\t      :dht (throw (ex-info (str \"a dht:<dir> store is opened by \"\n   190\t                                \"yin.repl.dht/open, which composes its node\")\n   191\t                           {:spec (dissoc checked :bind!)})))))\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t(defn durable?\n   195\t  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store: its published index\n   196\t   outlives the process, so a session rebuild continues it rather than\n   197\t   starting an empty one (dao.space.store/durable?).\"\n   198\t  [store]\n   199\t  (durable/durable? store))\n   200\t\n   201\t\n   202\t(defn close!\n   203\t  \"Release the store's lifecycle resources (dao.space.store/close!): the\n   204\t   content log and, in durable mode, the directory lock.  Idempotent.\"\n   205\t  [store]\n   206\t  (durable/close! store))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
