{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"diff -u <(git show HEAD:src/cljc/yin/repl/store/fs.cljc | tail -n +2) <(tail -n +2 src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc) | head -75; rg -n 'lock\"'!|unlock!|atomic-replace|held|fsync|claim|stale|worker'\"' src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc | head -120; nl -ba test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj | sed -n '20,315p'; rg -n 'yin-repl-node|test:clj|test:' bb.edn\"","aggregated_output":"--- /dev/fd/11\t2026-10-01 03:55:18\n+++ /dev/fd/13\t2026-10-01 03:55:18\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n   \"Explicit host file operations for the durable index store directory\n-   (docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md, the durable-store design's\n-   host section): an exclusive directory lock held by the one process\n+   (dao.space.store; docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md, the\n+   durable-store design's host section): an exclusive directory lock held by the one process\n    that owns the store, and an atomic write-temp, sync, rename\n    replacement for HEAD. CLJ, Node, and Dart each implement them with\n    their own primitives; nothing here falls back silently.\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:4:   durable-store design's host section): an exclusive directory lock held by the one process\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:12:   its core, so each contender creates its own uniquely named claim\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:17:   contenders never both own it (`node-lock!`) — two worker threads of\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:18:   one process included, since a claim naming this pid is live unless it\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:21:   Contract, pid reuse (Node only): a claim's liveness is its pid's, so a\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:22:   crashed owner's claim whose pid the OS has since given to an\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:25:   the claim entries it saw.  Operator remedy: confirm that no REPL uses\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc:28:   start o