release; closing whatever the host\n   229\t   needs closed is all releasing takes.\n   230\t\n   231\t   `claimed`, `(fn [])`, runs on Node once this process's claim entry\n   232\t   exists and before it reads the others — the window a concurrent\n   233\t   contender can race — so the tests can interleave one there.\"\n   234\t  ([dir] (lock! dir {}))\n   235\t  ([dir {:keys [claimed]}]\n   236\t   (let [key (canonical-dir dir)]\n   237\t     (when-not (claim! key)\n   238\t       (refuse-locked dir))\n   239\t     (let [release! (try (host-lock! dir (str dir \"/\" lock-name) claimed)\n   240\t                         (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   241\t                                   :clj Throwable\n   242\t                                   :cljs :default)\n   243\t                                e\n   244\t                           (swap! held disj key)\n   245\t                           (throw e)))\n   246\t           released? (volatile! false)]\n   247\t       {:release! (fn []\n   248\t                    (when-not @released?\n   249\t                      (vreset! released? true)\n   250\t                      (release!)\n   251\t                      (swap! held disj key)))}))))\n   252\t\n   253\t\n   254\t(defn unlock!\n   255\t  \"Release a lock `lock!` answered. Idempotent: a released lock releases\ntest/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:828:      (let [close! (durable/lock-releasing-close\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc:225:(defn- open-locked-dir\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc:269:(defn lock-releasing-close\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc:300:    (let [{:keys [handle lock recovery]} (open-locked-dir dir)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc:302:             :close-fn (lock-releasing-close (:close-fn handle) lock)\n-          (let [on-disk (dao.jing.file/records (store/content-path dir))]\n+          (let [on-disk (dao.jing.file/records (durable/content-path dir))]\n             (is (pos? (count on-disk)))\n             (is (contains? (into #{} (map first) on-disk)